<title>USA: Centigram off after terminating talks.</title>
<headline>Centigram off after terminating talks.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Centigram Communications Corp were off 1-5/8 to 12-1/8 after the company said it had terminated discussions about acquiring Voice-Tel Enterprises Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Due to current market conditions, the companies have decided not to proceed with the proposed acquisition at this time and will remain independent,&quot; the company said in a statement issued after the market closed Monday. &quot;Moving forward, we plan to continue our strong, long-term business relationship with Voice-Tel.&quot;</p>
<p>Centigram is a leading global provider of wireless and wireline messaging and communications solutions.</p>
